As part of our astronomical research at the observatory, we've compiled a significant dataset, "Stellar Observations," that we're continuously expanding with new data from telescopic captures. Currently, our dataset identifier is 'ds_12345'. This dataset has multiple versions due to series of enhancements and derivative analyses. We need to optimize the storage layout of this dataset to improve query efficiency, preferably reducing query time significantly, without exceeding our storage capacity limit of 500GB. It's crucial to maintain a derivative relationship between the dataset versions.

To ensure that the optimization aligns with the previous successful optimization which resulted in a 95% reduction in query time, using up to 480GB storage capacity, I would like to request the performance of an optimization function on our dataset.

Could you please call the function to optimize the storage layout for the dataset with ID 'ds_12345', setting the maximum storage capacity to 500GB and establishing a derivative relationship type, aiming for a similar reduction in query time and storage utilization?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
