I have a series of recorded customer service calls in English that I need to convert into written transcripts for a qualitative analysis project. The recordings are approximately 30 minutes in duration each. I require transcription with detailed accuracy, including punctuation, to maintain the integrity of the conversations. It's also important to identify when different customer service representatives take over the conversation, as well as to provide me with timestamps for each spoken word, so I can align the text with behavioral analysis. The audio files are stored online and can be accessed using URLs.

Can you transcribe the audio recordings into text, ensuring punctuation is included, speakers are identified, and word timestamps are provided? Here are the details you will need to proceed:

- URL of an example audio file: `https://example.com/audio/customer-service-call1.mp3`
- Language of the audio: English (BCP-47 code `en-US`)
- Punctuation: Enabled
- Speaker Diarization: Enabled
- Word Time Offsets: Enabled

I request you to use this information and transcribe the provided audio file using your speech-to-text API capabilities.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "transcribe_audio", "args": {"audio_url": "https://example.com/audio/customer-service-call1.mp3", "language_code": "en-US", "enable_automatic_punctuation": true, "enable_speaker_diarization": true, "enable_word_time_offsets": true}}]}
<|end|>


