I am currently working on bridging our Salesforce CRM system with the Pega Platform to streamline our customer management processes. We want to synchronize the customer data from our Salesforce instance to Pega to ensure consistent information across platforms. The Salesforce CRM is hosted at `https://mycompany.salesforce.com`. The data synchronization needs to happen with our Pega Platform instance, specifically the customer data endpoint `https://pega.mycompany.com/api/v1/data/customer`. I have the authentication details ready for both systems. For Salesforce, the client ID is `abc123`, client secret is `secret123`, the username is `user@example.com`, and the password is `password123`. For the Pega Platform, we will use the API key `pega-api-key-456`.

Please initiate the synchronization process using the `functions.sync_salesforce_data` function with the information provided to align our customer data between Salesforce CRM and Pega Platform.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "sync_salesforce_data", "args": {"salesforce_instance_url": "https://mycompany.salesforce.com", "pega_endpoint_url": "https://pega.mycompany.com/api/v1/data/customer", "authentication_details": {"salesforce": {"client_id": "abc123", "client_secret": "secret123", "username": "user@example.com", "password": "password123"}, "pega": {"api_key": "pega-api-key-456"}}}}]}
<|end|>


