To ensure the effectiveness of our production planning for the upcoming quarter, we need to create a detailed schedule that takes into account our various product lines, each with their own unique production requirements and deadlines. Specifically, we have two product lines that need to be scheduled. Product line A requires the use of machines M1 and M2 during the period from July 1st to July 15th, within labor shifts S1 and S2. The materials needed for this line are Material1 and Material2. Product line B will utilize machines M3 and M4 from July 16th to July 30th and will operate during shift S3, relying on materials Material3 and Material4 to meet production demands.

To accomplish this, we need to generate a production schedule that incorporates machine availability schedules for machines M1, M2, M3, and M4, labor shift schedules for shifts S1, S2, and S3, and the available supply of materials Material1, Material2, Material3, and Material4. Deadlines for each product line are also critical to ensure timely delivery.

Therefore, I am requesting a function call to generate this production schedule with the specifics provided. Here is the data for each function call argument:

Product Lines:
```markdown
| Product Line | Machine IDs  | Labor Shifts | Material IDs        | Start Date  | End Date    |
|--------------|--------------|--------------|---------------------|-------------|-------------|
| A            | M1, M2       | S1, S2       | Material1, Material2| 2023-07-01  | 2023-07-15  |
| B            | M3, M4       | S3           | Material3, Material4| 2023-07-16  | 2023-07-30  |
```

Machine Availability:
```markdown
| Machine ID | Availability Dates         |
|------------|-----------------------------|
| M1         | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15    |
| M2         | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15    |
| M3         | 2023-07-16 to 2023-07-30    |
| M4         | 2023-07-16 to 2023-07-30    |
```

Labor Shifts:
```markdown
| Shift ID | Shift Dates                |
|----------|----------------------------|
| S1       | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15   |
| S2       | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15   |
| S3       | 2023-07-16 to 2023-07-30   |
```

Material Supply:
```markdown
| Material ID | Supply Dates              |
|-------------|---------------------------|
| Material1   | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15  |
| Material2   | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15  |
| Material3   | 2023-07-16 to 2023-07-30  |
| Material4   | 2023-07-16 to 2023-07-30  |
```

Deadlines:
```markdown
| Product Line | Deadline Date  |
|--------------|----------------|
| A            | 2023-07-15     |
| B            | 2023-07-30     |
```

With this data, please execute the function to generate the production schedule that is fully compliant with the constraints and deadlines of each product line.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "generate_production_schedule", "args": {"product_lines": "| Product Line | Machine IDs  | Labor Shifts | Material IDs        | Start Date  | End Date    |\n|--------------|--------------|--------------|---------------------|-------------|-------------|\n| A            | M1, M2       | S1, S2       | Material1, Material2| 2023-07-01  | 2023-07-15  |\n| B            | M3, M4       | S3           | Material3, Material4| 2023-07-16  | 2023-07-30  |", "machine_availability": "| Machine ID | Availability Dates         |\n|------------|-----------------------------|\n| M1         | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15    |\n| M2         | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15    |\n| M3         | 2023-07-16 to 2023-07-30    |\n| M4         | 2023-07-16 to 2023-07-30    |", "labor_shifts": "| Shift ID | Shift Dates                |\n|----------|----------------------------|\n| S1       | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15   |\n| S2       | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15   |\n| S3       | 2023-07-16 to 2023-07-30   |", "material_supply": "| Material ID | Supply Dates              |\n|-------------|---------------------------|\n| Material1   | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15  |\n| Material2   | 2023-07-01 to 2023-07-15  |\n| Material3   | 2023-07-16 to 2023-07-30  |\n| Material4   | 2023-07-16 to 2023-07-30  |", "deadlines": "| Product Line | Deadline Date  |\n|--------------|----------------|\n| A            | 2023-07-15     |\n| B            | 2023-07-30     |"}}]}
