As we continue to improve the efficiency of our baggage handling system at our airline, we anticipate a high passenger volume for flight AA123 on April 22, 2023. To effectively manage the baggage flow and minimize wait times at the carousel, we need to predict the baggage volume for this flight and assign it to the optimal number of carousels. Additionally, for enhanced customer satisfaction, we aim to provide real-time tracking of checked baggage for selected passengers. We have previous flight data indicating that on a similar weekday, flight AA123 roughly handled 350 pieces of luggage.

I request the execution of the following function calls with the provided parameters:
1. Predict the baggage volume for flight AA123 on April 22, 2023.
2. Assign the predicted baggage volume to the available carousels for optimal flow.
3. Track the real-time status of the baggage with the following unique identifiers: ['BG001', 'BG002', 'BG003', 'BG004'].

Given this setup, could you please initiate the appropriate function calls to manage these tasks?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
