Our company needs to standardize the process of exchanging various types of documents with our suppliers, such as converting CSV files into the EDI format and securely transmitting them. For instance, we have a CSV file located at "path/to/source_file.csv" that needs to be converted to an EDI file and then sent to our supplier's endpoint at "https://supplier.example.com/edi-receiver".

Please call the `convert_to_EDI` function to convert this CSV file into the EDI format. After the conversion is successful and we have the converted file at "path/to/converted_file.edi", call the `transmit_EDI` function to transmit the EDI formatted file to our supplier's endpoint. We are looking to automate this exchange process for purchase orders and invoices to enhance our operational efficiency.

The specific details for the function call are as follows:
- CSV file location to convert: "path/to/source_file.csv"
- Target format after conversion: "EDI"
- Path for the converted EDI file: "path/to/converted_file.edi"
- Supplier endpoint URL for transmission: "https://supplier.example.com/edi-receiver"

Please return confirmation of conversion and transmission success upon completion of the function calls.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "convert_to_EDI", "args": {"file_path": "path/to/source_file.csv", "target_format": "EDI"}}]}
<|end|>


