I recently developed a smart home application that enables users to control their home environment via voice commands. To enhance the user experience, I am looking to integrate Siri for voice-activated lighting and temperature control. I envision users being able to say phrases like "Hey Siri, turn on the living room lights" or "Hey Siri, set the temperature to 72 degrees" to interact with the smart home system. Could you set up the voice command integration in my app using Siri, with specific commands for lighting and thermostat adjustments? The voice commands for the light control should include variations such as "turn on the lights," "switch off the bedroom lights," and "dim the kitchen lights to 50%." For the thermostat, the voice commands should include "set the temperature to 68 degrees," "increase the thermostat by 5 degrees," and "lower the temperature in the bedroom."

The result I'm aiming for is successful integration messages confirming that Siri can now manage these smart home features, as indicated by the function call results. Please call the necessary functions with these details to set up Siri integration for lighting and thermostat control within my smart home application.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "integrateSiriLightControl", "args": {"commands": ["turn on the lights", "switch off the bedroom lights", "dim the kitchen lights to 50%"]}}]}
<|end|>


