To assist with streamlining pharmaceutical R&D processes, I require a detailed analysis of clinical trial data for a new medication intended to treat chronic inflammation. The specific clinical trial has generated a substantial dataset detailing patient responses, biomarker levels, and safety outcomes. I have the dataset accessible at `https://clinicaltrials.gov/data/trial_data_inflammation_study.csv` and I seek statistical analysis to understand treatment efficacy and safety profiles.

I'm also looking to predict potential side effects for our lead compound, with its molecular structure detailed in the file located at `https://pharmainfo.com/compound_structure.json`. For this, I would like to employ a deep learning-based prediction model to anticipate and mitigate risks effectively.

Lastly, an optimized dosing strategy is crucial for maximizing therapeutic benefits while minimizing adverse reactions. Patient demographics, including age, weight, and genetic markers, have been compiled into a JSON file `https://patientinfo.com/patient_data.json`, alongside drug properties such as bioavailability and half-life available at `https://drugdata.com/drug_properties.json`. I aim to find the optimal dosing regimen based on these inputs to ensure personalized and safe treatment.

Please use the provided data to call the necessary functions to perform these analyses and identify optimal dosing strategies.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "analyze_clinical_trial_data", "args": {"trial_data": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/data/trial_data_inflammation_study.csv", "analysis_type": "statistical"}}]}
<|end|>


