I am developing a feature for an e-learning platform that will help students learn Shakespearean literature by listening to famous passages. I've selected the passage "To be, or not to be, that is the question" from Hamlet, which needs to be converted into an audio file. I require this to be read in a high-quality British English accent and saved in MP3 format to be compatible with our platform. This audio piece needs to sound natural, as if an experienced actor is delivering the line on stage. 

Could you please call the speech synthesis function to convert the given text into spoken audio using a British English voice and export the audio in MP3 format? Here are the specifics for the function call to synthesize speech:

- Text to be converted to speech: "To be, or not to be, that is the question."
- Desired voice and accent for the speech synthesis: British English (en-GB)
- Audio format: MP3

This audio will be a critical component of our interactive module to enhance the learning experience for the students, so I need the quality to be top-notch. Thank you.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "list_voices", "args": {"language": "en-GB"}}]}
<|end|>


