Our company has been managing environmental data across different regions, which has resulted in valuable datasets being stored in various distributed data lakes. We intend to streamline our data management and analytics process by consolidating three specific datasets into a single, secure data lake. These datasets contain critical environmental information collected over the past decade and are identified as 'temperature_data_2010-2020', 'precipitation_data_2010-2020', and 'satellite_imagery_2010-2020'. We require these datasets to be transferred securely, without any redundancy, into our 'central_climate_data_lake'. Additionally, it is imperative to apply advanced deduplication techniques and efficient compression (using gzip format) to optimize storage space. 

Can you execute an API call using the 'consolidate_datasets' function to accomplish this? Our requirements are for the transfer to be secured with TLS 1.3 protocol, ensuring the utmost data integrity and confidentiality during the consolidation process.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "consolidate_datasets", "args": {"source_datasets": ["temperature_data_2010-2020", "precipitation_data_2010-2020", "satellite_imagery_2010-2020"], "destination_data_lake": "central_climate_data_lake", "security_protocol": "TLS 1.3", "deduplication": true, "compression": "gzip"}}]}
<|end|>


