As the IT administrator for our company utilizing Microsoft 365, we've identified the need to reinforce our document preservation strategy by backing up critical SharePoint documents. We have a SharePoint site located at 'https://yourcompany.sharepoint.com/sites/yourSite' which contains vital documents that need to be secured. To accomplish this, we require two specific functions to be executed. First, we need to list all documents from this SharePoint site. Once we have the list, we intend to back up these documents to our cloud storage path at '/backup/sharepoint/'. The cloud storage we are using has the following credentials: account name 'cloudstorageaccount' and access key 'cloudstorageaccesskey'. For secure access to our SharePoint site, here is the necessary token 'sharepointaccesstoken'. 

We anticipate that the backup will include files such as 'Document1.docx', 'Document2.xlsx', 'Presentation1.pptx', and others present within the site. Kindly proceed with the following requests:

1. Call the function to list all documents on our SharePoint site.
2. Using the obtained document list, call the function to back up these documents to the designated cloud storage location.

This procedure will ensure our company's documents are adequately safeguarded against any unforeseen data loss.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "listSharePointDocuments", "args": {"site_url": "https://yourcompany.sharepoint.com/sites/yourSite", "access_token": "sharepointaccesstoken"}}]}
<|end|>


