I am currently overseeing a project where we utilize Trello for task management. We've encountered the need to streamline our issue reporting process, and as part of this effort, I would like to integrate our issue tracking system with Trello. Specifically, when a team member reports a new issue in our system, I want a Trello card to be automatically created and placed in the 'Backlog' list on our 'Development' board. 

To facilitate this, the Trello card should include detailed information such as the title of the issue, a comprehensive description, and the name of the individual who reported it. For instance, if a bug is found in our software, the issue title might be "Login Functionality Bug," and the description would elaborate on the problem, including steps to reproduce it and any error messages encountered. The reporter's name, let's say "Jane Doe," would be attributed on the Trello card to ensure accountability and traceability.

I would like to request the creation of this integration, ensuring that our workflow remains unobstructed and that the relevant team members can promptly address any reported issues. 

Could you set up this integration for our Trello board using the details provided?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "create_trello_card_integration", "args": {"board_name": "Development", "list_name": "Backlog", "issue_title": "Template for Issue Title", "issue_description": "Template for Issue Description, including steps to reproduce and error messages.", "reporter_name": "Template for Reporter Name"}}]}
<|end|>


