I need to ensure a smooth data synchronization process between our customer relationship management (CRM) system and support ticketing platform using Zapier workflows. However, we are frequently hitting the rate limit of the ticketing system's API, resulting in errors. To address this issue, I'd like a function to be called that implements a retry mechanism equipped with exponential backoff. The specifics should include an initial delay of 2 seconds before the first retry attempt, a maximum of 5 retry attempts, and a multiplier of 2 to increase the delay after each attempt.

Furthermore, I require a function to promptly notify our admin team when a critical error, such as the 'API rate limit exceeded', has occurred. Notifications should be sent via email to 'admin@example.com'. This will allow our team to be aware and potentially take necessary actions beyond the automated retry mechanism.

