I am analyzing a dataset from our supply chain operation that tracks the dealings between various suppliers and manufacturers. The dataset includes specific identifiers for companies, details of transactions, and product shipment records. I need to extract the relationships between these entities in a structured format. Here is a sample extract from our records in a supply chain document:

| supplier_id | manufacturer_id | transactions                        |
|-------------|-----------------|-------------------------------------|
| S12345      | M54321          | [{transaction_id: "T001", product_id: "P123", quantity: 100, date: "2023-03-15"}, {transaction_id: "T002", product_id: "P124", quantity: 200, date: "2023-03-17"}] |
| S12346      | M54322          | [{transaction_id: "T003", product_id: "P125", quantity: 150, date: "2023-03-16"}, {transaction_id: "T004", product_id: "P126", quantity: 250, date: "2023-03-18"}] |

I would like to request the use of the appropriate functions to process these records and represent the extracted connection data between suppliers and manufacturers in a JSON schema format. This extracted relationship data will then be integrated into our supply chain management system for further analysis and reporting. Can you help me with this extraction?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "extract_supplier_manufacturer_relationships", "args": {"supply_chain_data": [{"supplier_id": "S12345", "manufacturer_id": "M54321", "transactions": [{"transaction_id": "T001", "product_id": "P123", "quantity": 100, "date": "2023-03-15"}, {"transaction_id": "T002", "product_id": "P124", "quantity": 200, "date": "2023-03-17"}]}, {"supplier_id": "S12346", "manufacturer_id": "M54322", "transactions": [{"transaction_id": "T003", "product_id": "P125", "quantity": 150, "date": "2023-03-16"}, {"transaction_id": "T004", "product_id": "P126", "quantity": 250, "date": "2023-03-18"}]}], "output_schema": true}}]}
<|end|>


