I would like to create an Amazon S3 bucket specifically for this project. The bucket should be private to maintain data confidentiality and should be located in the US West (Oregon) region to optimize latency for our analysis teams. The bucket will be named "project-dataset-storage."

Additionally, to manage storage costs effectively, I want to set up a lifecycle policy for this S3 bucket. The policy should transition objects to the S3 Infrequent Access storage class 30 days after the upload date. Furthermore, after 90 days, the objects should be transitioned to the S3 Glacier storage class for more cost-effective long-term storage.

Please assist me by executing the following function calls:
1. Create the private S3 bucket named "project-dataset-storage" in the "us-west-2" region.
2. Configure the lifecycle policy for the "project-dataset-storage" S3 bucket with the specified transition rules.

To ensure complete setup, I request to call the `create_s3_bucket` and `configure_lifecycle_policy` functions with the parameters outlined above.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "create_s3_bucket", "args": {"bucket_name": "project-dataset-storage", "region": "us-west-2", "access_control": "private"}}]}
<|end|>


