I am working on a Databricks project titled "Data Aggregation and ML Model Execution" which requires processing voluminous datasets stored within an Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 container located at `https://mydatalake.dfs.core.windows.net/lakehouse/data/`. The job entails two primary tasks: the first is to aggregate data, potentially using Apache Spark SQL queries for performance, and the second is to train a machine learning model using Databricks MLlib on the aggregated dataset. I need to ensure the job is continually optimized for performance considering the large size of the datasets involved.

To execute this job, I require the creation of a Databricks job with the following specifics:

- Name of the job: "Data Aggregation and ML Model Execution"
- Task Descriptions:
  1. Task to aggregate data from specified Azure Data Lake paths.
  2. Task to run a machine learning model on the aggregated data.
- Dependencies: The ML model execution task should depend on the completion of the data aggregation task.
- Libraries: Include libraries required for Apache Spark SQL and Databricks MLlib.
- Notifications: Set up email notifications to alert me at `data.team@company.com` upon job start, success, and failure.
- Cluster Configuration: Utilize a cluster optimized for big data processing and machine learning workloads.

I would like to proceed with creating this job to automate data processing tasks. Please assist me in setting up the Databricks job execution according to the details provided.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls": [{"name": "create_job", "args": {"name": "Data Aggregation and ML Model Execution", "tasks": [{"task_key": "aggregate_data", "description": "Task to aggregate data from specified Azure Data Lake paths using Apache Spark SQL.", "notebook_path": "/Notebooks/aggregate_data"}, {"task_key": "run_ml_model", "description": "Task to run a machine learning model on the aggregated data using Databricks MLlib.", "notebook_path": "/Notebooks/run_ml_model", "depends_on": ["aggregate_data"]}], "max_retries": 3, "timeout_seconds": 10800, "libraries": [{"library_type": "maven", "coordinates": "org.apache.spark:spark-sql_2.12:3.1.1"}, {"library_type": "maven", "coordinates": "org.apache.spark:spark-mllib_2.12:3.1.1"}], "email_notifications": {"on_start": ["data.team@company.com"], "on_success": ["data.team@company.com"], "on_failure": ["data.team@company.com"]}}}]}
<|end|>


