own wizard, and no soft drinks (or wizards) are left out. How exciting. This is a perfectly bijective function, also called a **bijection**. Again, the only way to get a bijection is for the domain and codomain to be the same size (although that alone does not _guarantee_ a bijection; witness f 5 , above). Also observe that if they _are_ the same size, then injectivity and surjectivity go hand-in-hand. Violate one, and you're bound to violate the other. Uphold the one, and you're bound to uphold the other. There's a nice, pleasing, symmetrical elegance to the whole idea. 
