24. What's the binary number     10110011101010102 in hexadec-     imal? Or is that too hard a     question to eyeball? 
 Naw, it's easy. By inspection, it's B3AA 16 , since each of the four 4-bit nibbles goes one-for-one with a hex digit. (You can look up nibble values on p. 181 if you want, but again it's definitely worth memorizing.) 
