Definition IDV Independent and Dependent Variables Suppose A is the augmented matrix of a consistent system of linear equations and B is a row-equivalent matrix in reduced row-echelon form. Suppose j is the index of a pivot column of B. Then the variable xj is dependent. A variable that is not dependent is called independent or free.  
