 Example NM A nonsingular matrix, Archetype B Example HUSAB shows that the coefficient matrix derived from Archetype B, specifically the 3 x 3 matrix, 
 B = 
 [- 7 - 6 - 12 5 5 7 1 0 4 
 ] 
 is a nonsingular matrix since the homogeneous system, LS(B, 0 ) , has only the trivial solution. 4 Notice that we will not discuss Example HISAD as being a singular or nonsingular coefficient matrix since the matrix is not square. The next theorem combines with our main computational technique (row reducing a matrix) to make it easy to recognize a nonsingular matrix. But first a definition. Definition IM Identity Matrix The m x m identity matrix, Im, is defined by 
